# Git safety

- Branch policy lives in `.vibeops.json` (`integrationBranch`, `productionBranch`).
- `vibeops task add` creates `task/*` from the **integration** branch (e.g. `develop`).
- Include the TASK id in commit messages, e.g. `feat(task-015): short title`.
- **`vibeops task done`** pushes the branch and opens an MR/PR — it does **not** merge locally.
- Merge on GitHub/GitLab; CI deploys after merge. No force-push to shared branches.
